# Every environment variable of Legible Consulting's estate, by name. No values. One audit file,
# written 2026-10-23 from GitHub Actions (gh secret list, gh variable list), Vercel (the REST API,
# teams kodominio and remi21), each repo's own .env.example on main, the blueprint at v0.7.0, the
# local machine and the cloud environment. core/stack.md names the machines; desk/mani.yaml names
# the estate. The blueprint's template/.env.example and .icm/uat/CONTEXT.md set the canonical
# names of a UAT build: VERCEL_TOKEN, VERCEL_TEAM, VERCEL_PROJECT, NEON_API_KEY, NEON_PROJECT_ID,
# DATABASE_URL, DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED.
#
# How to read this file. One section per place a value lives. In a section, one line per name. The
# note above a name says what it holds, which projects or repos use it, and where to set it. A name
# that lives in several places has one line in each section. Never write a value here. A value
# lives in Vercel, in a repository's Actions secrets and variables, in ~/.zshrc or in the cloud
# environment dialog, and never in git.
#
# Where to set a value:
#   Vercel    the project > Settings > Environment Variables. Or, in the repo's clone:
#             vercel env add NAME <environment> --scope kodominio
#             <environment> is production, preview, development or the custom environment's slug.
#   Actions   gh secret set NAME --repo <owner>/<repo>
#             gh variable set NAME --repo <owner>/<repo> --body "<value>"
#   Local     export NAME=... in ~/.zshrc, or NAME=... in front of one command.
#   Cloud     claude.ai/code > the environment `legible` > Environment variables.
#
# Vercel projects. Team kodominio: berceo (k0d0minio/berceo), agorasim (k0d0minio/agorasim, root
# web/), vinecliff (k0d0minio/vinecliff), legible-desk (legible-consulting/house, root desk/app/),
# portfolio, client-referrals and jamie-nisbet (k0d0minio/jamienisbet, roots websites/portfolio,
# websites/sellers-site, websites/admin-dashboard). Team remi21: app, admin, marketing,
# documentation, support and demo (k0d0minio/remi-ai, roots apps/*). site-proof has no Vercel
# project. berceo and agorasim carry the custom environment `uat`; no other project does.
# remi-ai keeps its own catalogue of every name in .icm/docs/ENV.md.
#
# "The Neon set" below means the eighteen names the Neon integration (Storage > Neon) writes on
# every project that has a database. They hold four facts: the pooled connection string, the
# direct one, the Neon Auth URL and the Neon project id. The code reads DATABASE_URL; berceo and
# legible-desk also read NEON_AUTH_BASE_URL. Never set one of them by hand: the integration
# rewrites them, and a deleted one comes back on its next sync.


# ===== Vercel: production =====================================================================

# --- The Neon set. Projects: berceo, agorasim, vinecliff, legible-desk, portfolio,
# client-referrals, jamie-nisbet, remi21/app, remi21/admin. Set by the integration. ---
# The pooled connection string of the production branch. The one name the code reads.
DATABASE_URL=
# The direct (unpooled) connection string of the same branch, for migrations.
DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED=
# The Neon Auth URL of the branch. berceo and legible-desk read it.
NEON_AUTH_BASE_URL=
# The Neon project's id. An identifier, not a secret.
NEON_PROJECT_ID=
# libpq parts of the pooled string: database, pooled host, direct host, password, user.
PGDATABASE=
PGHOST=
PGHOST_UNPOOLED=
PGPASSWORD=
PGUSER=
# The same connection under the legacy Vercel Postgres names. Nothing in the estate reads them.
POSTGRES_DATABASE=
POSTGRES_HOST=
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=
POSTGRES_PRISMA_URL=
POSTGRES_URL=
POSTGRES_URL_NON_POOLING=
POSTGRES_URL_NO_SSL=
POSTGRES_USER=
# The Neon Auth URL again, under the name a Vite client reads. Nothing in the estate reads it.
VITE_NEON_AUTH_URL=

# --- Set by hand, per project. ---
# Bearer token of the scheduled routes (/api/cron/*). berceo (D-68: one value on every environment
# and in the Actions secret of the same name), agorasim. A rotation touches every copy.
CRON_SECRET=
# Resend API key. berceo, agorasim, portfolio, client-referrals. Each project holds its own copy.
# The team also holds a shared variable of this name, linked to escondidinho only (not estate).
RESEND_API_KEY=
# The sender address for Resend. berceo. remi-ai apps/marketing documents it and has none set.
EMAIL_FROM=
# Signs the Neon Auth session cookie: openssl rand -base64 32. berceo, legible-desk.
NEON_AUTH_COOKIE_SECRET=
# Stripe secret key: live on production, test everywhere else. berceo, agorasim, jamie-nisbet.
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
# Signing secret of this environment's Stripe webhook endpoint. berceo, agorasim.
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# Neon Object Storage for the professionals' documents (S3-compatible, one private bucket per
# Neon project; DOCUMENTS_S3_* because Vercel reserves AWS_*). berceo.
DOCUMENTS_S3_ENDPOINT=
DOCUMENTS_S3_REGION=
DOCUMENTS_BUCKET=
DOCUMENTS_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
DOCUMENTS_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# HMAC key that signs the admin session cookie. agorasim, jamie-nisbet.
ADMIN_SESSION_SECRET=
# The owner password of the dashboard login. jamie-nisbet. On agorasim the login reads admin_users
# and the code no longer reads this name (web/.env.example); the agorasim copy is left over.
ADMIN_PASSWORD=
# Vercel Blob store: token, store id, webhook public key. Set by Storage > Blob. agorasim,
# remi21/app, remi21/admin.
BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=
BLOB_STORE_ID=
BLOB_WEBHOOK_PUBLIC_KEY=
# Booking mail: the From address, the team's notification addresses (comma-separated). agorasim.
BOOKING_EMAIL_FROM=
BOOKING_NOTIFICATION_EMAILS=
# Signs the per-booking cancellation tokens. agorasim (production and uat, not preview).
BOOKING_TOKEN_SECRET=
# Keys the opt-out list of the post-tour mail. Never rotate it: every stored opt-out is a hash
# under it. agorasim.
EMAIL_OPT_OUT_SECRET=
# The deployment's own origin: Stripe return URL, mail assets, canonicals. agorasim.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=
# Stripe Connect: the client's account id (acct_...), not a key. agorasim.
STRIPE_CONNECTED_ACCOUNT_ID=
# Stripe publishable key, handed to the browser at request time. agorasim.
STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
# Stripe publishable key, inlined at build. jamie-nisbet.
NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
# Signs the admin session cookie. vinecliff, remi21/app, remi21/admin.
AUTH_SECRET=
# The one address allowed to create the first operator account. remi21/app, remi21/admin.
OPERATOR_EMAIL=
# Fine-grained GitHub token for the house only: Contents, Pull requests, Actions read and write.
# legible-desk.
DESK_PAT=
# Fine-grained GitHub token per client-repo owner: Contents, Actions, Metadata, Commit statuses,
# Pull requests read; Pull requests write for the gates. ESTATE_PAT is k0d0minio's,
# ESTATE_PAT_<OWNER> one more owner. legible-desk.
ESTATE_PAT=
ESTATE_PAT_SUSTENTUS=
# The bearer the portfolio's contact form sends to the desk's /api/pool: openssl rand -hex 32.
# One value, the same name, on legible-desk and portfolio. desk/CONTEXT.md and desk/app/.env.example
# still call the portfolio's copy DESK_POOL_TOKEN; Vercel holds POOL_TOKEN on both.
POOL_TOKEN=
# The pool API's address, for the portfolio's form. portfolio.
DESK_POOL_URL=
# Vercel AI Gateway key. portfolio, jamie-nisbet.
AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY=
# GitHub token. portfolio: read-only Contents on the private icm-board repo. jamie-nisbet: repo
# scope, for client repos and the tickets board.
GITHUB_TOKEN=

# --- Documented in a repo's .env.example and set on no Vercel environment (2026-10-23). The code
# treats most of them as optional; agorasim's backup store is required in practice. ---
# agorasim: the private Blob store of the nightly database backup; Sentry; retention periods.
BACKUP_BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=
SENTRY_DSN=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=
ENQUIRY_RETENTION_DAYS=
AUDIT_IP_RETENTION_DAYS=
# vinecliff: transactional mail and the public origin.
RESEND_FROM=
# remi-ai apps (team remi21): each app's own base URL and the addresses of the other apps.
# marketing also documents EMAIL_FROM and RESEND_API_KEY and holds no variable at all.
APP_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_ADMIN_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_MARKETING_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_DOCS_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPPORT_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_DEMO_URL=
# jamie-nisbet: optional overrides.
GITHUB_REPO_OWNER=
PORTFOLIO_BASE_URL=


